D = {
 "Abbathor|MTF": "The dwarf god of greed, who teaches that hunger for wealth keeps a clan strong and safe. He prefers theft to honest crafting and nudges dwarves toward shortcuts, which sometimes turn into better methods. His followers hoard treasure and see taking it by cunning as a virtue.",
 "Amaunator|FRHOF": "God of the sun, law, and kept promises. He is stern and orderly, and his faithful believe he dies and is reborn again and again. People swear oaths, sign contracts, and declare laws in his name, and some argue that Lathander is only one of his aspects.",
 "Arawai|ERLW": "Sovereign of Life and Love in the Sovereign Host. She is the patron of fertility and the gentle side of nature, bringing good harvests and kind rain to those who honor her.",
 "Arms of the Betrayers|EGW": "Eight sentient weapons forged by Betrayer Gods from the life force of greater fiends, scattered across Wildemount by the Calamity. Each bound fiend gathers its own cult of worshipers. A found weapon lends its wielder some of the god's power, and the fiend within pursues its own goals.",
 "Arvoreen|MTF": "The halfling god of vigilance and defense. Halfling children hear tales of his bravery and clever tactics and act them out as games, which trains them for the day their home needs protecting. His followers guard villages and use speed and small size against bigger foes.",
 "Asmodeus|EGW": "Devil god of tyranny and domination who rules the Nine Hells from the fortress of Nalsheem. His honeyed words corrupt mortal hearts, and his punishments are the stuff of nightmares. Evil beings and many warlocks pay him tribute.",
 "Asmodeus|SCAG": "Lord of the Nine Hells, worshiped openly only in recent generations. His cult rose after the Spellplague by offering answers and forgiveness to people who felt abandoned. His devils are silver-tongued tempters who trade in bargains and contracts, and the cult still struggles for acceptance.",
 "Athreos|MOT": "The River Guide, god of passage, who ferries the dead across the Tartyx River to their fate in the Underworld. He is no judge. He reads each soul, carries it to its proper place, and offers no haggling and no sympathy. Mortals see him as the mystery of life's last moment.",
 "Aureon|ERLW": "Sovereign of Law and Lore in the Sovereign Host. He is called the first wizard and shared the secrets of wizardry with the world. Scholars, sages, and spellcasters honor him.",
 "Auril|FRHOF": "The cold, merciless goddess of winter. She freezes beauty in magical ice and keeps it for herself, and she speaks through icy whispers or messengers like yetis. People in harsh northern lands, such as Icewind Dale, pray to her with offerings so she will spare them.",
 "Avandra|EGW": "She Who Makes the Path, goddess of freedom, travel, trade, and adventure. Her shrines stand beside roads rather than in cities. Merchants, free spirits, and adventurers revere her, and taverns toast her as a giver of luck and fortune.",
 "Azuth|FRHOF": "The First Magister, god of spells and spellcasting and the right hand of Mystra. Where Mystra is raw force, Azuth gives that force form. His priests teach that casters should approach the Art with devotion and care, and they believe meditation on his sayings brings new insight.",
 "Baervan Wildwanderer|MTF": "Gnome god of forests and travelers, a peaceful wanderer whose trips turn into adventures. His mischievous giant raccoon companion, Chiktikka Fastpaws, causes most of the trouble. He knows every plant and bird song, never gets lost, and can befriend nearly anyone.",
 "Bahamut|EGW": "The Platinum Dragon, pillar of justice, protection, nobility, and honor. Metallic dragons revere him as the first of their kind, and paladins of order and good look to him. To follow him is to look after those who cannot look after themselves.",
 "Bahgtru|VGM": "Orc god of brute strength and ruthless force, who drives every blow an orc strikes. Myths tell of him laughing as a giant behir wrapped around him and treating that grip as the ultimate test of might. His followers fight savagely and fear nothing.",
 "Balinor|ERLW": "Sovereign of Horn and Hunt in the Sovereign Host. He guides both beast and hunter and patronizes those who live on the edge between civilization and the wild.",
 "Bane|EGW": "Evil god of war and conquest, the Strife Emperor. His blood-soaked armies crush foes and force the weak to bow. Warmongering nations and goblinoid tribes worship him, and he plots from the fortress of Banehold in Acheron.",
 "Bane|FRHOF": "God of tyrants and ambition who teaches that the strong have a duty to rule the weak. A ruler who grows soft or corrupt should be replaced by a stronger one. He is one of the Dead Three with Bhaal and Myrkul and has returned to greater prominence than before.",
 "Baravar Cloakshadow|MTF": "Gnome goddess of illusion and deception. She taught gnomes to hide, use magic, and fool their enemies. After escaping a goblin god's trap, she began wearing a new face each time and following a different routine each day so no one can predict her.",
 "Berronar Truesilver|MTF": "Dwarf goddess of home, family, honor, and law. Her code sets dwarven contracts, trade agreements, and every bond made by word or deed. Her priests arrange marriages meant to strengthen each generation, and their word on this is sacred.",
 "Beshaba|SCAG": "Goddess of bad luck and the dark counterpart of Tymora. She is cruel and capricious, and people name her when misfortune strikes or speak to her to ward off her notice. Folk offer her propitiation so she does not turn her attention their way.",
 "Bhaal|FRHOF": "God of murder who delights in ritual killing and the dread it spreads. He values the fear and paranoia a hidden killer causes as much as the act itself. He is one of the Dead Three with Bane and Myrkul, and a red handkerchief marks his manifestations.",
 "Boldrei|ERLW": "Sovereign of Hall and Hearth in the Sovereign Host. She guides and protects communities and families and inspires people to work together for the common good.",
 "Branchala|DSOTDQ": "The Bard King, god of music, poetry, and the inner beauty of living things. Many elves and kender worship him above other gods. He is a champion of life and laughter who brings solace and joy through song.",
 "Brandobaris|MTF": "Halfling god of stealth and a trickster, the star of wild tales full of narrow escapes. Children play at his exploits, and some grow into adventurers who live as he does, always seeking the next challenge. He is the patron of thieves and daring wanderers.",
 "Callarduran Smoothhands|MTF": "Deep gnome god who led his people into the Underdark and taught them to survive there. He embodies the drive to examine everything closely and make discoveries. He stole the heart of the earth lord Ogremoch and polished it smooth, gaining power over earth elementals.",
 "Ceratos|EGW": "A many-minded being from the Far Realm, one of the oldest creatures in Exandria, who loves chaos. Ceratos sleeps beneath the ground with scattered thoughts. They offer magic to those who spread chaos on the surface, hoping to regain their full power one day.",
 "Charmalaine|MTF": "Halfling goddess of luck and quick escapes, a spontaneous adventurer who expects to sense danger and dodge it. Tales say she escaped sahuagin armies and solved the Chamber of a Thousand Traps. She is called the Lucky Ghost for her ability to send out her spirit.",
 "Chauntea|FRHOF": "The Grain Goddess, the most widely worshiped god among common folk in Faerun. She governs agriculture, hearth, and home, and city dwellers pray to her at meals and births. She prefers quiet acts of devotion to grand displays and rarely appears to mortals.",
 "Chemosh|DSOTDQ": "God of undeath and false redemption who tempts followers with the promise of eternal life. Those who accept find that they live on while their bodies rot. His worshipers embrace his grim reputation by wearing white skull masks and black robes.",
 "Chislev|DSOTDQ": "God of nature on its own terms, ruling the cycles of life that go on regardless of mortal acts. Enigmatic and shy, Chislev fiercely protects all plants and animals as their children. Hermits and druids revere nature without asking for anything back.",
 "Clangeddin Silverbeard|MTF": "Dwarf god of battle and patron of dwarf warriors, brave and impetuous yet a cunning strategist. He urges his followers to leave the stronghold and destroy goblinoids, giants, and dragons before they become a threat. His faithful are full-time warriors trained from youth.",
 "Corellon|EGW": "Guardian of spring, beauty, and the arts, patron of arcane magic and the fey. Corellon seeded the world with the first arcane magic and is considered the parent of all elves. Those who seek art in their work honor Corellon and despise the Spider Queen for leading the drow astray.",
 "Corellon Larethian|MTF": "Creator of all elves, as changeable as a breeze, quick to anger and quick to forgive. Corellon loves magic, art, nature, and freedom. The god asks for no strict ritual, only that followers enjoy life, try new things, pursue their dreams, and be kind.",
 "Cyric|FRHOF": "Power-hungry god of strife, chaos, and malicious deception. He tricks people into ruinous acts and wants everyone afraid and divided. A mortal who became a god by killing Bhaal, he later helped bring about the Spellplague. He is petty and megalomaniacal.",
 "Cyrrollalee|MTF": "Halfling goddess of friendship, hospitality, and the home. Halflings honor her by welcoming visitors and treating a host's house as if it were their own, while the home itself stays sacrosanct. Her best-known legend is the tale of her troll pies.",
 "Deep Duerra|MTF": "Duergar goddess of psionics, said to have stolen that power from mind flayers and enslaved a whole colony of them. Her priests lead attacks on dwarves and mind flayers, and every duergar stronghold keeps a training ground where all must learn combat basics.",
 "Deep Sashelas|MTF": "Elf god of the sea, seafaring, and knowledge, called the Knowledgeable One. Sea elves and elf sages love him most. Sailors toss gold and jewels overboard to ask for calm storms and fair winds, and he is inclined to help even those not fully devoted.",
 "Dendar|VGM": "The Night Serpent, born from the feverish dreams of the first thinking beings. She grows stronger by feeding on fear. Her followers believe she will eventually devour the world, and yuan-ti worshipers are led by nightmare speakers.",
 "Deneir|FRHOF": "God of reading and writing, and of any image meant to convey truth. He is Oghma's scribe and is often shown as scatterbrained. He speaks to mortals through books, with words rearranging themselves or a quill writing on its own. His work is behind Faerun's high literacy.",
 "Desirat|EGW": "A fiendish phoenix once the mount and companion of Asmodeus, now chained beneath the Cyrios Mountains. Her shadowed flames have scarred the land above for centuries. Isolation has fractured her mind and fed delusions of divinity, which she spreads to her worshipers.",
 "Dol Arrah|ERLW": "Sovereign of the Sun and Honor in the Sovereign Host. She drives away darkness and stands for wisdom in war, honorable fighting, justice, and sacrifice for the greater good.",
 "Dol Dorn|ERLW": "Sovereign of Strength and Steel in the Sovereign Host. He is the patron of the common soldier and guides anyone who holds a weapon. He stands for courage, strength, and martial skill.",
 "Eilistraee|FRHOF": "Drow goddess of dance, song, beauty, moonlight, swordplay, and hunting, and the child of Lolth and Corellon Larethian. She is a hope for drow who oppose the Spider Queen. She urges followers to choose their own destiny, even if that means leaving the Underdark for the surface.",
 "Eilistraee|MTF": "Drow goddess who would lead Lolth's worshipers to the surface. Most drow know nothing of her, as matron mothers guard her scrolls in order to know their enemy. Raiders are told to retreat when they see the moon, since her lure is strongest under its light.",
}
